{
  "info": {
    "name": "Auth Service",
    "description": "End-to-end API collection for the auth-service (OAuth 2.0).\n\n## Variables\n\n| Variable | Default | Description |\n|----------|---------|-------------|\n| `baseUrl` | `http://localhost:8080` | Local app base URL. Set to the deployed API Gateway URL (e.g. `https://<api-id>.execute-api.<region>.amazonaws.com`) when testing a deployed environment. |\n| `clientId` | `user-service` | OAuth client name sent via HTTP Basic auth. Seeded by `scripts/init_localstack.py` in the e2e environment. |\n| `clientSecret` | `client-secret` | Client secret matching the seeded `user-service` registration. |\n| `e2eUserEmail` | `root@example.com` | Email served by the user-service mock for the password grant. |\n| `e2ePassword` | `e2e-password` | Password accepted by the user-service mock. |\n| `accessToken` | *(empty)* | Latest access token — set automatically by the token-response test scripts. |\n| `refreshToken` | *(empty)* | Latest refresh token — set automatically by the password/refresh grant test scripts. |\n| `authCode` | *(empty)* | Authorization code — set automatically by the \"Authorize\" test script. |\n\n## Notes\n\n- The token endpoint accepts `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` bodies.\n- The client-credentials and authorization-code grants authenticate the client with an HTTP Basic `Authorization` header (`clientId:clientSecret`).\n- `/oauth/revoke` and `/oauth/authorize` require a `Bearer` access token issued by this service.\n- The password grant is deprecated per OAuth 2.1; responses carry a `Warning` header.\n- The authorize request uses the RFC 7636 Appendix B PKCE verifier/challenge pair.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Liveness probe — no authentication required. Returns {\"status\": \"healthy\"}."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('responds with 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('reports healthy status', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.eql({ status: 'healthy' });",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "OAuth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Token — client credentials",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Basic {{basicAuth}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/oauth/token",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "oauth",
                "token"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                {
                  "key": "grant_type",
                  "value": "client_credentials"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Client credentials grant (RFC 6749 Section 4.4). Returns a service token for the seeded `user-service` client. The test script stores the access token in the `accessToken` variable."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('basicAuth', btoa(`${pm.collectionVariables.get('clientId')}:${pm.collectionVariables.get('clientSecret')}`));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('responds with 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('returns a bearer token with the granted scope', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.token_type).to.eql('Bearer');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.access_token).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(body.scope).to.eql('users:read');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('expires in the configured service token lifetime', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.expires_in).to.eql(30);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('disables response caching', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Cache-Control')).to.include('no-store');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', body.access_token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Token — client credentials with invalid secret",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Basic {{basicAuthInvalid}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/oauth/token",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "oauth",
                "token"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                {
                  "key": "grant_type",
                  "value": "client_credentials"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Wrong client secret must be rejected with `invalid_client` (RFC 6749 Section 5.2) and a `WWW-Authenticate: Basic` header."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('basicAuthInvalid', btoa(`${pm.collectionVariables.get('clientId')}:wrong-secret`));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('responds with 401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                  "pm.test('returns invalid_client error', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.eql('invalid_client');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('challenges for basic auth', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('WWW-Authenticate')).to.eql('Basic');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Token — client credentials with unauthorized scope",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Basic {{basicAuth}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/oauth/token",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "oauth",
                "token"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                {
                  "key": "grant_type",
                  "value": "client_credentials"
                },
                {
                  "key": "scope",
                  "value": "users:write"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Requesting a scope the client is not registered for must fail with `invalid_scope`."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('basicAuth', btoa(`${pm.collectionVariables.get('clientId')}:${pm.collectionVariables.get('clientSecret')}`));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('responds with 400', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('returns invalid_scope error', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.eql('invalid_scope');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Token — unsupported grant type",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
